+# PRIVATE, unapproved technical shape
+
+The only runtime edits are the native-generated root package property, its exact three lock registration lines and the unchanged native patch. This is a separate change from Stage B source work. The current R16 package/lock are the authenticated native base: minimal insertions produce the existing native hashes, and inverse insertions recover the complete current bytes. No fresh bookkeeping generation is necessary or allowed by this packet.
+
+## Version and artifact boundary
+
+The registration selects nested `@ark/schema@0.56.2`; top-level0.56.0 remains unchanged. ArkType2.2.3 and the qualified util/resolution/integrity identities remain fixed. Patch SHA256 is `95380ed9b554038220bc538ec54cb02834a0a3134e391b4a195358338fbbec1c`; only package-relative `out/scope.js` changes. The derived `.bun-tag-35e6c4b58501c484` is installer bookkeeping and is excluded from repository source. Later materialization checks all105 canonical files plus that exact marker, not a `.bun-*` wildcard. Its observed mode0664 belongs to the retained campaign premise, not a universal tool guarantee.
+
+## Existing qualified algorithm
+
+`precompileReferences` builds the current ID→object map and a per-call eligibility map. A node must already have precompilation and belong outside the owning scope, unless no owning scope is supplied. Own Allows/Apply functions, and Optimistic for every union, are required; a broken compiled-callback invariant throws before publishing borrowed slots.
+
+Eligibility also requires exact current ID/object membership, no alias/cyclic node and a reusable complete non-self `referencesById` closure. Marking a node visiting before recursion forces nonalias cycles to fall back. Ineligible dependencies and same-ID different objects prevent borrowing for affected nodes. The unchanged original emitters generate their callbacks. There is no second optimizer or expanded eligibility rule.
+
+For eligible nodes, registry references publish exact existing bound callbacks into every required slot. They already carry their old table as receiver; `bindPrecompilation` retains existing external bindings. Scope export passes `this` as owning scope so owned nodes generate and rebind into the scope's new table even when previously compiled. All union Allows/Apply/Optimistic slots remain required.
+
+## Ownership and measured limits
+
+Registry references strongly retain the borrowed callbacks; bound functions retain their old compiled tables. Fewer emitted functions and lower observed RSS increment do not imply less retained heap or shorter lifetime. No weak table, eviction, GC scheduling or retention mechanism is introduced or qualified.
+
+Historical fixed memory readings were C381/379/384MB versus B509/513MB. All C readings passed the unchanged strict<500MB assertion; both B expected failures remain. This measures rounded RSS increment after HTTP shape import relative to the child after ArkType import, not total/peak RSS or512MiB pod headroom.
+
+The fixed validation workload pooled median ratio was1.130153967375641, within its declared1.20 aggregate budget. Raw Standard Schema was40.164781% slower. These measurements retain their original fixture/environment/corpus scope; no new sampling, tuning or retention claim is authorized.
+
+## Evidence transfer and maintenance
+
+The native-generation receipt and accepted two-materialization audit are provenance for exactly these unchanged artifacts. Original reproduction stage remains FAILED; its separate successful continuation supplies the second materialization and finite fault/diagnostic evidence. Existing mechanism/semantic/type/producer/structural/memory/cost results apply only to their exact input hashes. R16 source differences do not inherit old candidate-suite acceptance.
+
+WBS contracts maintainers own target/canonical pins, patch compatibility review and removal. Upstream replacement, a version change, lost canonical identity, failed candidate semantics or an unacceptable tradeoff triggers removal or separately reviewed replacement. Removal deletes the property, exact lock registration and patch together, then verifies ordinary stock resolution and complete normal candidate checks. Reversibility does not confer adoption authority.
+
+All exact integrated-candidate checks listed in tasks.md remain pending. MAIN, PR630, deployment and adoption remain held; this private draft creates no accepted ADR or new domain term.
